+# Unified desktop Settings
+
+Both desktops put Settings, Restart and Shut Down in the existing bottom-right
+control row. Node keeps its status and clock controls above the row. Its Settings
+gear opens the same modeless Settings instance as the Home card; Wi-Fi and
+Ethernet remain available under Network Connections.
+
+Node retains its nine existing Settings categories and adds Display Settings.
+Vault has the relevant local categories: Display Settings, Keyboard and Mouse,
+Date & Time, and Backup and Restore. The latter opens the existing Vault Wallet
+Backup and Decrypt Backup tools. It does not introduce a second backup format.
+
+## Display integration
+
+The shared `core_display_settings.DisplaySettingsDialog` runs in the desktop
+process. Saved Node layouts are restored before automatic display scaling at
+session startup. A session-owned watcher handles connection changes. Both
+sessions pass their product explicitly to `core-display-scale` and own the
+watcher PID through logout. Settings children follow remaining screens after a
+primary-screen change, unplug, or resolution reduction.
+
+Home refreshes the current launch environment from `core_display` before opening
+applications. Reopened GTK applications therefore receive the confirmed
+`GDK_SCALE`/`GDK_DPI_SCALE` values without restarting the desktop session. The
+display component owns the 15-second Keep/Revert transaction, rollback worker,
+layout validation, and display-profile persistence.
+
+## Portable device profiles
+
+The Settings footer offers Export device settings and Import device settings in
+both products. A versioned JSON document contains only:
+
+- Keyboard layout/model/variant/options and bounded repetition/Num Lock settings.
+- Supported pointer settings associated with device names.
+- An optional validated saved display profile.
+
+Wallets, arbitrary filesystem paths, commands, passwords, network settings and
+clock timestamps are excluded. Unknown fields, duplicate keys, files over
+128 KiB, symlinks and special input files are rejected. Export creates a new file
+with mode 0600 and refuses to overwrite an existing file.
+
+Opening a profile validates and previews it. Applying input settings is a
+separate action. Reviewing a display profile stages its choices in Display
+Settings; it never applies a screen layout or saves it without the display
+confirmation flow. A source product may differ from the target product.
+
+The installed Node saves its input preferences through its existing supported
+keyboard and input backends. Vault saves only in its verified private RAM home;
+explicit export to USB is the way to retain a device profile across sessions.
+The device profile is separate from a Node configuration backup.
+
+## Verification
+
+`tests/test_device_profiles.py` exercises the profile boundary, unsafe inputs,
+non-overwrite export and validation before side effects.
+`tests/test_unified_settings.py` opens the real Home/Settings widgets offscreen,
+checks single-instance gear navigation and compact layouts, simulates recovery
+of an off-screen dialog, and verifies the refreshed launch environment.
+Existing Settings navigation, footer, status and guide contracts remain in use.
+
+Offscreen tests do not prove physical display/driver behavior. The release VM
+matrix must also exercise Keep, Revert, timeout, output unplug, Node reboot
+persistence, and Vault session reset before claiming an ISO is ready.
